      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/office-addins/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="001" status="pending">Installed node_modules, the measured per-file error breakdown, and the per-directory rollup row for shared/taskpane/** that sizes this task. Do not start before 001's report exists; without it there is no way to prove at the end that no error was displaced into another task's directory.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/** ONLY. Do NOT edit any file under shared/adapters/**, shared/services/**, shared/__mocks__/**, word/** or outlook/** — tasks 007 and 008 own those and run concurrently with this one. A cross-boundary edit is both a merge conflict and a lost fix. If a shared/taskpane error can only be fixed by changing a file outside this directory, STOP and escalate rather than reaching across.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: every fix in this task. Fix types PROPERLY. MUST NOT use `any`, `as any`, `as unknown as T`, `@ts-ignore`, `@ts-expect-error`, or a blanket non-null assertion (`!`) applied merely to silence a diagnostic. MUST NOT relax src/client/office-addins/tsconfig.json — `strict`, `exactOptionalPropertyTypes`, `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`, `noUnusedLocals` and `noUnusedParameters` all stay exactly as they are. tsconfig.json is OUT OF SCOPE for this task and for 007 and 008. A suppressed error is not a cleared error; FR-18 exists so that NEW errors are visible in Phases 1 through 3, and a suppression re-hides them.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: every fix in this task. This is a TYPE-LEVEL change only. MUST NOT change runtime behaviour: no altered conditional, no changed default value, no reordered or added/removed effect, no changed hook dependency array semantics, no renamed prop that alters the rendered DOM or the props a consumer passes, no deleted branch. `noUnusedLocals` and `noUnusedParameters` errors are the trap here — deleting an "unused" variable that is actually a side-effecting call, or an unused parameter that shifts the positional signature of a callback, IS a runtime change. Prefer prefixing an intentionally unused parameter with an underscore over deleting it. If an error can only be resolved by a behaviour change, STOP and escalate.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: the three known barrel defects (shared/taskpane/index.ts lines 3 and 18; shared/taskpane/components/views/index.ts line 2). For each missing type, first determine whether it exists under another name or in another module — if so, correct the re-export to point at the real declaration. If it does not exist at all, REMOVE the broken re-export. MUST NOT invent a placeholder type, an empty interface, or a stub union merely to satisfy the barrel: that converts a visible defect into an invisible lie and gives Phase 1 a type that means nothing. If any consumer imports the missing name, that consumer is also broken — fix it (it is inside this directory) and record it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: the `ViewType` finding specifically. FR-03 (task 015) will extend `NavigationTab` and build the Save and Find tab shell. `ViewType` may be an intended-but-never-created union. RECORD that finding for task 015 in your notes; do NOT pre-build the tab type system here. Scope expansion into FR-03 is out of bounds for a typecheck task.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">SCOPE: any JSX or styling you touch while fixing a type. Fluent UI v9 only, and the Office theme continues to drive light/dark via the existing `useOfficeTheme` / `useTheme` hooks. MUST NOT introduce a hardcoded colour, a raw hex value, or a non-Fluent component while resolving a type error.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">SCOPE: import resolution while fixing types. This project holds a recorded Path A exception (project CLAUDE.md Decisions, 2026-09-04): the add-in keeps thin views under shared/taskpane/ and consumes `@spaarke/auth` only. MUST NOT resolve a missing type by importing from `@spaarke/ui-components` — its components assume a different React posture and some are Xrm-bound, which breaks at runtime in an Office host (NFR-03).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: dependencies. MUST NOT add, remove or upgrade any npm dependency to satisfy a type, and MUST NOT modify package.json or package-lock.json. If a type error stems from a missing or wrong `@types` package, STOP and escalate — a dependency change alters what every other task compiles against.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">SCOPE: test files under shared/taskpane/**/__tests__/. These are inside the tsconfig include globs, so their errors count toward this task. Fix their types the same way as production code. MUST NOT delete, skip or `xit` a test to make typecheck pass — that is a KEEP-path violation under docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md. If a test's type error reveals that the test asserts something the code no longer does, STOP and escalate.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE: build verification. `npm run build` IS the production build in this package — there is no `build:prod` script (package.json line 7). Do not attempt `npm run build:prod`; src/client/office-addins/CLAUDE.md line 39 names it in error.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>TypeScript strict-mode remediation; React 19 plus Fluent UI v9 in an Office task pane</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/plan.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/typecheck-baseline.md</file>
      <file>src/client/office-addins/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-021-fluent-design-system.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-012-shared-components.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/ui/fluent-v9-host-visual-fit.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="exactOptionalPropertyTypes — the two correct fixes" location="src/client/office-addins/tsconfig.json line 21">Under this option, `prop?: T` means "may be absent", NOT "may be undefined". Two legitimate fixes: (1) if the property genuinely may hold `undefined`, widen the DECLARATION to `prop?: T | undefined` — this is honest and is usually right for React props threaded from optional state; (2) if the property should simply be absent, fix the CALL SITE with a conditional spread such as `...(value !== undefined ? { prop: value } : {})`. Choose per case based on what the consumer means. Never widen to `any` and never cast the object.</pattern>
      <pattern name="noUncheckedIndexedAccess — narrow, do not assert" location="src/client/office-addins/tsconfig.json line 20">An index access yields `T | undefined`. Fix by narrowing — a guard, a default via `??`, optional chaining, or destructuring with a default — not by appending `!`. A non-null assertion here is exactly the class of "fix" that turns a compile-time signal into a runtime crash inside an Office webview, where the failure surfaces as a blank pane with no console the user can reach.</pattern>
      <pattern name="noUnusedLocals / noUnusedParameters — the side-effect trap" location="src/client/office-addins/tsconfig.json lines 16-17">Before deleting an unused binding, check whether its initialiser has a side effect (a subscription, a registration, a hook call). Deleting `const x = doSomething()` deletes the call. For an unused function parameter that must stay for positional reasons, prefix with an underscore rather than removing it. This is the single most common way a "type-only" change becomes a behaviour change.</pattern>
      <pattern name="displacement check" location="projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/typecheck-baseline.md">Because 006, 007 and 008 run concurrently on the same package, a fix in one directory can surface or move an error into another. At the end of this task, re-run the full typecheck and compare the counts for shared/adapters, shared/services, word and outlook against the task 001 baseline rows. They must not increase. If they do, that is your fix leaking across a boundary — resolve it inside your own directory or escalate.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Office theme is the dark-mode source" location="src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/hooks/useOfficeTheme.ts">ADR-021's dark-mode requirement is satisfied in this package by the Office host theme driving the Fluent provider. The ui-test below toggles the Office theme rather than an app-level switch — verify the hook still supplies the theme after any type change in the provider chain.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Emit the mandatory rigor declaration (RIGOR LEVEL: FULL, reason, protocol steps). Load projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/CLAUDE.md, spec.md FR-18, and projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/typecheck-baseline.md. Record this task's starting error count for shared/taskpane/** and the baseline counts for the four directories you do NOT own.</step>
    <step order="1">Ensure src/client/office-addins/node_modules exists. If it does not (a fresh shell), run `npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund` — a bare `npm install` fails with ERESOLVE. Then revert package-lock.json if npm rewrote it.</step>
    <step order="2">Resolve the three known barrel defects first, because they are real broken public surface and because their resolution may change the error counts elsewhere in the directory: `ViewType` at shared/taskpane/index.ts line 3, `SaveOptions` at shared/taskpane/index.ts line 18, and `SaveOptions` at shared/taskpane/components/views/index.ts line 2. For each, search for the type's real declaration; correct the re-export if it exists, remove it if it does not. Fix any in-directory consumer of the removed name. Record what you found for each.</step>
    <step order="3">Work the remaining errors file by file, highest count first per the task 001 breakdown. Apply the fix patterns in the knowledge block; for each distinct error code, settle on one canonical fix shape and apply it consistently across the directory so the diff is reviewable.</step>
    <step order="4">Re-run `npm run typecheck` and filter to shared/taskpane/**. Iterate until that filter is empty.</step>
    <step order="5">Run the displacement check: re-run the full typecheck and compare the per-directory counts for shared/adapters, shared/services, shared/__mocks__, word and outlook against the task 001 baseline. None may increase. Record the comparison.</step>
    <step order="6">Run `npm run build` (the production build; there is no build:prod) and confirm it is green.</step>
    <step order="7">Run `npm test` and confirm the suite is green with no test deleted, skipped or weakened relative to the task 001 baseline counts.</step>
    <step order="8">Execute the ui-tests below in a dev build against a host (or the mock-office harness where a live host is unavailable) and record the result of each, including the dark-mode check.</step>
    <step order="9">Write projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/typecheck-fix-patterns.md recording, per error code, the canonical fix shape you used and any case where you deviated and why. Tasks 007 and 008 follow this so all three diffs look like one change. Also record the `ViewType` finding for task 015 (FR-03).</step>
    <step order="9.5">Run the Step 9.5 quality gates (code-review plus adr-check) per the FULL rigor level. The review's primary question is not "does it compile" but "did any of these edits change behaviour" — direct it at deleted bindings, changed defaults, altered conditionals and modified hook dependency arrays.</step>
    <step order="10">Update projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to completed.</step>
    <step order="11">Document any deviation from this task file in projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a typecheck error in shared/taskpane/** can only be resolved by editing a file outside that directory, STOP and escalate per root CLAUDE.md section 6. Tasks 007 and 008 own those files and are running concurrently; reaching across produces a merge conflict and silently discards one of the two fixes. Report the error, the file that would need to change, and which task owns it.</trigger>
    <trigger>If a typecheck error can only be resolved by changing runtime behaviour — altering a conditional, a default value, an effect, or a rendered output — STOP and escalate. This task's contract is type-level only. A behaviour change smuggled in under a typecheck task is invisible to review and will be attributed to whichever Phase 1-3 task lands next.</trigger>
    <trigger>If a test file's type error reveals that the test asserts behaviour the code no longer has, STOP and escalate rather than deleting, skipping or rewriting the assertion (ADR-038 KEEP-path rules). That is a real defect finding, not typecheck debt.</trigger>
    <trigger>If clearing this directory requires adding, removing or upgrading an npm dependency (including a missing `@types` package), or relaxing any tsconfig option, STOP and escalate. Both change what every other task in the package compiles against.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the actual error count for shared/taskpane/** differs materially from the task 001 baseline row when you start, STOP and reconcile before working — either the baseline is stale or another task has already touched this directory, and both are worth knowing before a large mechanical diff.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Word task pane renders after type remediation">
      <steps>
        <step>Run `npm run build` in src/client/office-addins and load the Word add-in in a dev build (or run `npm run start:word`).</step>
        <step>Open the Spaarke task pane in Word.</step>
        <step>Observe the shell: header, footer, and the Save surface.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The pane renders with no blank screen and no error boundary. The browser console shows no new uncaught exception relative to the pre-change build. The Save surface is present and interactive exactly as before the change.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Outlook task pane renders after type remediation">
      <steps>
        <step>Load the Outlook add-in in a dev build (or run `npm run start:outlook`).</step>
        <step>Open the Spaarke task pane on a mail item.</step>
        <step>Exercise the navigation between the visible tabs and open the Create To Do view.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The pane renders, navigation works, and the Create To Do view opens and displays its fields. No error boundary is triggered and no new console exception appears. Outlook is the host with the most shared/taskpane surface in use today, so it is the stronger regression signal of the two.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="ADR-021 dark mode via Office theme toggle">
      <steps>
        <step>With the pane open, switch the Office host theme from light to dark (Office Account settings, Office Theme, or the host's dark-mode toggle).</step>
        <step>Observe the pane without reloading it, then reload the pane and observe again.</step>
        <step>Switch back to light and repeat.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The pane follows the Office theme in both directions, via the existing `useOfficeTheme` / `useTheme` hooks. Text remains legible against its background in both themes, no element keeps a light-mode background in dark mode, and no hardcoded colour has been introduced by the type fixes (ADR-021).</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Keyboard navigation and announcements unchanged">
      <steps>
        <step>With the pane open, tab through the shell from the first focusable element to the last.</step>
        <step>Trigger a state change that uses the existing `useAnnounce` pattern (for example a save or a validation error).</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Focus order and visible focus rings are unchanged from before the task, every interactive element remains reachable by keyboard, and the announcement still fires (NFR-11). A dropped announcement would indicate a deleted "unused" binding.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">`npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund` if needed; `npm run typecheck`; `npm run build` (production — there is no build:prod); `npm test`; `npm run start:word` / `npm run start:outlook` for the ui-tests.</tool>
    <tool name="Grep">Locate the real declarations of `ViewType` and `SaveOptions`, and find consumers of any re-export you remove.</tool>
