  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a completed `npm install`, when `npm run typecheck` is run in src/client/office-addins and the output is filtered to paths under shared/taskpane/, then zero errors are reported.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the same typecheck run, when the per-directory counts for shared/adapters/, shared/services/, shared/__mocks__/, word/ and outlook/ are compared against the task 001 baseline, then none has increased.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`npm run build` exits 0.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`npm test` exits 0 with suite and test counts greater than or equal to the task 001 baseline — no test was deleted, skipped or replaced with a weaker assertion.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Each of the three known barrel defects is resolved by either pointing the re-export at a real declaration or removing it, and projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/typecheck-fix-patterns.md records which resolution was applied to each and why.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: `grep` across the diff finds no newly added `any`, `as any`, `as unknown as`, `@ts-ignore` or `@ts-expect-error` in shared/taskpane/**.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: `git diff` shows src/client/office-addins/tsconfig.json, package.json and package-lock.json unmodified.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: `git diff --name-only` lists no file under shared/adapters/, shared/services/, shared/__mocks__/, word/ or outlook/.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no placeholder, stub or empty type was introduced to satisfy a barrel re-export.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no import from `@spaarke/ui-components` was added (ADR-012 Path A exception, NFR-03).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: the diff introduces no hardcoded colour or non-Fluent-v9 component (ADR-021).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All four ui-tests below pass and their results are recorded, including the dark-mode check in both directions.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/typecheck-fix-patterns.md exists, records a canonical fix shape per error code, and records the `ViewType` finding for task 015 (FR-03).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The Step 9.5 code-review and adr-check gates ran and their findings are resolved or explicitly accepted.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec reference: FR-18 (line 92), NFR-04 (line 101), NFR-11 (line 108), Success Criterion 12 (line 209). Plan reference: section 4 Phase 0 tasks 006-008, risk R-6.

No `&lt;justification&gt;` block is present: this is a modify-only task. It adds no new service, abstraction, endpoint, DI registration, package or column — CLAUDE.md section 11's gate does not apply to edits of existing files.

Parallel-safety within the P0-typecheck wave: 006 owns shared/taskpane/**, 007 owns shared/adapters/** plus shared/services/** (and shared/__mocks__/** if task 001 reports it as the only UNASSIGNED residue), 008 owns word/** plus outlook/**. The three directory sets are disjoint, so the three tasks can run concurrently without touching the same file. The shared risks are (a) all three run `npm run build` and `npm test` against the same node_modules, and (b) all three may edit projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/typecheck-fix-patterns.md — this task CREATES that file and 007/008 append to it, so write it early and keep sections clearly headed by task id. tsconfig.json is out of scope for all three, which removes the one file they would otherwise contend for.

Sizing note: shared/taskpane contained 56 .ts/.tsx files at authoring time — the largest of the three buckets by file count. The task 001 rollup, not this note, is the authority on the error count.</notes>

